      ":question/id": "a9aa3ffa-4834-541b-babc-7d728ab4346e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{- 7 x - 3 y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{- 7 x - 3 y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x^{2}\\left(\\frac{- 7 x - 3 y}{x}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x (- 7 x - 3 y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 7 x^{2} - 3 x y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(3 x)}_{P(x)}y=\\underbrace{- 7 x^{2}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 3 x y=- 7 x^{2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=3 x$ and $Q(x)=- 7 x^{2}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3865e8e6-fa47-5660-8790-ee947653c12c",
